 "text": "Hi, how you holding up? The simple one is a tablecloth. Drape it over the table and bugs can't land on it. They do attract some bugs, but they kill them with heat. A chipped pot of hot water does the same thing but without the smell. A few drops of alcohol kill them and they stay put. A shot glass full of vinegar does the trick too. Much better. A plastic bottle you can throw away is cheaper, too. A tall glass of rice or a plate of sugar also keeps them away.",
